-- Glasshouse: the rules of the ledger.
--
-- This file says which facts the ledger may hold and how they may
-- change. Every write is checked against it. A write that breaks a rule
-- is refused, and the refusal names the rule.
--
-- How to read it:
--   predicate       the shape of a fact (a "claim")
--   invariant       a rule that every claim must satisfy, always
--   define          a named condition, reused below
--   transformation  an act: the only way claims are added or removed
--   require         a gate: the act is refused unless this holds
--   admit, retract  add a claim, remove a claim
--   actor           whoever is making the proposal
--
-- Three habits run through the file:
--   * Every business fact starts with its organisation. Tenants are
--     separated by the shape of the facts, not by a filter.
--   * Permissions are claims too. They are granted by an act, so every
--     grant is on the record.
--   * Nothing is overwritten. A correction adds a new version and links
--     it to the old one. The old one stays.
--
-- Times are UTC instants. Daylight saving is handled outside the ledger.
-- A curve's prices are stored outside too. The ledger holds their hash.

program glasshouse

-- Who may do what. Each is granted by an act further down.
predicate MayCaptureTrade(actor: Subject, org: Subject, book: Subject)
predicate MayRegisterCurve(actor: Subject, org: Subject, market: Subject)
predicate MayValueTrade(actor: Subject, org: Subject, book: Subject)
predicate MaySetLimit(actor: Subject, org: Subject)
-- Who may hand out the permissions above, in one organisation.
predicate MayGrantAuthority(actor: Subject, org: Subject)
-- Who may create organisations. One holder: the ledger's root.
predicate MayEstablishOrganisations(actor: Subject)

-- Morpholog reads these two itself. Once an actor is restricted, only
-- the named database login may act as it. Anyone else is refused before
-- the rules run.
predicate ActorAssertionRestricted(actor: Subject)
predicate ActorAssertionAuthority(actor: Subject, login_role: Subject)

-- The currency a market's prices and valuations are in. Set once, when
-- the market is declared, and never changed. This is the one place a
-- currency comes from: a trade or a curve takes its market's.
-- A currency is a field here, not a unit like MW, because a unit is
-- fixed for a whole predicate and a currency differs from market to
-- market.
predicate MarketCurrency(org: Subject, market: Subject, currency: Subject)
    unique by (org, market)
    append only

-- A trade's identity. It never changes. Direction and counterparty are
-- part of what the trade is.
predicate TradeCaptured(org: Subject, book: Subject, trade: Subject, counterparty: Subject, market: Subject, direction: Subject)
    unique by (trade)
    append only

-- A trade's economic terms, one claim per version. An amendment adds a
-- version. `effective by` gives us `trade_terms_in_force_on`: the
-- version in force for a trade on a date. `partial` allows dates with
-- no version (before the trade date).
-- The price is per MWh, in the currency of the trade's market (see
-- MarketCurrency). It is a ratio, so it carries no unit here.
predicate TradeTerms(org: Subject, trade: Subject, version: Subject, quantity: Decimal[MW], price: Decimal, delivery_start: Timestamp, delivery_end: Timestamp, effective_from: Date)
    unique by (version)
    effective by (trade) on (effective_from) partial
    append only

-- Which terms version replaced which. A version is replaced at most once.
predicate TradeTermsSupersedes(new_version: Subject, prior_version: Subject)
    unique by (prior_version)
    append only

-- One version of a price curve for a market and date. The prices live
-- outside the ledger. `payload_hash` pins them.
predicate CurveRegistered(org: Subject, market: Subject, as_of: Date, version: Subject, payload_hash: Subject)
    unique by (version)
    append only

-- The curve version to use for a market and date. Exactly one at a time.
-- A correction moves the pointer and records what it replaced.
predicate OfficialCurve(org: Subject, market: Subject, as_of: Date, version: Subject)
    current pointer by (org, market, as_of)
    superseded via CurveSupersedes
predicate CurveSupersedes(new_version: Subject, prior_version: Subject)
    append only

-- One mark-to-market result. It names the exact curve version and terms
-- version it was computed from, so a later correction never changes a
-- number someone already saw. It states its currency, which must be
-- the currency of the trade's market.
predicate TradeValued(org: Subject, book: Subject, trade: Subject, curve_version: Subject, terms_version: Subject, mtm: Decimal, currency: Subject)
    unique by (trade, curve_version, terms_version)
    append only

-- A book's cap on its net position (bought less sold) in any one hour.
-- One cap per book. Not append only: a new cap replaces the old one, and
-- the audit log keeps every cap that ever stood.
predicate PositionLimit(org: Subject, book: Subject, cap: Decimal[MW])
    unique by (org, book)

-- Rules that hold for every claim, whichever act wrote it.
-- (Uniqueness, the single official pointer and the version chains are
-- generated from the clauses on the predicates above.)
--
-- A note for editors: a rule is re-checked for the claims its pattern
-- names. Name the claim's unique key (`trade`, `version`) even when the
-- rule does not use it. Then a write re-checks one claim, not every
-- claim that shares a value, and concurrent writers do not collide.

-- The currencies European power markets are priced in. A closed list,
-- so a mistyped code cannot become a market's currency for good.
-- Adding one is a change to this file.
invariant currency_is_one_power_is_priced_in:
    MarketCurrency(org: org, market: market, currency: currency)
    implies (currency = #EUR or currency = #GBP or currency = #NOK or currency = #SEK
        or currency = #DKK or currency = #PLN or currency = #RON)

invariant direction_is_buy_or_sell:
    TradeCaptured(trade: trade, direction: direction, ..)
    implies (direction = #buy or direction = #sell)

invariant position_limit_is_positive:
    PositionLimit(org: org, book: book, cap: cap) implies cap > 0 MW

invariant terms_belong_to_captured_trade:
    TradeTerms(org: org, trade: trade, ..) implies TradeCaptured(org: org, trade: trade, ..)

invariant quantity_is_positive:
    TradeTerms(trade: trade, version: version, quantity: qty, ..) implies qty > 0 MW

invariant delivery_period_is_ordered:
    TradeTerms(trade: trade, version: version, delivery_start: delivery_start, delivery_end: delivery_end, ..)
    implies delivery_start strictly_before delivery_end

-- The official pointer names a version registered for that same
-- organisation, market and date.
invariant official_curve_is_registered:
    OfficialCurve(org, market, as_of, version)
    implies CurveRegistered(org: org, market: market, as_of: as_of, version: version, ..)

invariant valued_trade_was_captured:
    TradeValued(org: org, book: book, trade: trade, ..)
    implies TradeCaptured(org: org, book: book, trade: trade, ..)

invariant valuation_curve_is_registered:
    TradeValued(org: org, curve_version: version, ..)
    implies CurveRegistered(org: org, version: version, ..)

invariant valuation_terms_version_is_registered:
    TradeValued(org: org, trade: trade, terms_version: version, ..)
    implies TradeTerms(org: org, trade: trade, version: version, ..)

-- A version replaces a version of the same trade.
invariant terms_lineage_stays_within_the_trade:
    TradeTermsSupersedes(new_version, prior_version)
    and TradeTerms(org: org, trade: trade, version: new_version, ..)
    implies TradeTerms(org: org, trade: trade, version: prior_version, ..)

-- Deliberately not rules: "a mark uses the official curve" and "a mark
-- uses the terms in force". Both are checked once, when the mark is
-- admitted (see admit_valuation). A mark records what was computed
-- then. A later correction or amendment must not make it unlawful.

-- Named conditions.

-- The terms in force on a date, for every trade of one organisation.
-- It picks the same version as the generated `trade_terms_in_force_on`.
-- The difference is the key. The generated one is looked up by trade.
-- The limit check finds its trades as it runs, so through the generated
-- one it would read every organisation's terms, and two organisations
-- capturing at the same moment would collide. This one is looked up by
-- organisation, which the act knows from the start.
define org_terms_in_force_on(org, as_of, trade, quantity, delivery_start, delivery_end):
    TradeTerms(org: org, trade: trade, quantity: quantity, delivery_start: delivery_start, delivery_end: delivery_end, effective_from: from, ..)
    and from on_or_before as_of
    and not (exists later: TradeTerms(org: org, trade: trade, effective_from: later, ..) and later after from and later on_or_before as_of)

-- Would the book stay within its cap in hour `h`? Adds up what the
-- book has bought and sold for that hour, under the terms in force on
-- `as_of`, then adds the proposed quantity (negative for a sale). The
-- trade named `amended` is left out: an amendment replaces its own
-- earlier quantity. A new trade is not in the book yet, so naming it
-- changes nothing.
define hour_is_within_cap(org, book, as_of, amended, signed_quantity, h, cap):
    abs(sum(q | org_terms_in_force_on(org, as_of, t, q, s, e)
                and TradeCaptured(org: org, book: book, trade: t, direction: #buy, ..)
                and t != amended and s at_or_before h and h strictly_before e)
        - sum(q | org_terms_in_force_on(org, as_of, t, q, s, e)
                and TradeCaptured(org: org, book: book, trade: t, direction: #sell, ..)
                and t != amended and s at_or_before h and h strictly_before e)
        + signed_quantity) <= cap

-- The acts. Every gate has a name, and a refusal reports that name.

-- Runs once, when the database is provisioned. The caller becomes the
-- root: it may create organisations, and only its own database login
-- may act as it from then on.
transformation establish_ledger(login_role):
    require ledger_is_new: not MayEstablishOrganisations(..)
    admit MayEstablishOrganisations(actor)
    admit ActorAssertionRestricted(actor)
    admit ActorAssertionAuthority(actor, login_role)

-- Create an organisation. The root can grant permissions in it.
transformation establish_organisation(org):
    require may_establish_organisations: MayEstablishOrganisations(actor)
    require organisation_is_new: not MayGrantAuthority(org: org, ..)
    admit MayGrantAuthority(actor, org)

-- Let someone else grant permissions in an organisation. They are tied
-- to one database login in the same act. Otherwise anyone could claim
-- to be them and grant themselves anything.
transformation grant_grant_authority(principal, org, login_role):
    require may_grant_authority: MayGrantAuthority(actor, org)
    admit MayGrantAuthority(principal, org)
    admit ActorAssertionRestricted(principal)
    admit ActorAssertionAuthority(principal, login_role)

transformation grant_capture_authority(principal, org, book):
    require may_grant_authority: MayGrantAuthority(actor, org)
    admit MayCaptureTrade(principal, org, book)

transformation grant_curve_authority(principal, org, market):
    require may_grant_authority: MayGrantAuthority(actor, org)
    admit MayRegisterCurve(principal, org, market)

transformation grant_valuation_authority(principal, org, book):
    require may_grant_authority: MayGrantAuthority(actor, org)
    admit MayValueTrade(principal, org, book)

transformation grant_limit_authority(principal, org):
    require may_grant_authority: MayGrantAuthority(actor, org)
    admit MaySetLimit(principal, org)

-- Declare a market and the currency it is priced in. Done once per
-- market, by whoever may grant permissions in the organisation. Trades
-- and curves in a market are refused until it is declared.
transformation declare_market(org, market, currency):
    require may_grant_authority: MayGrantAuthority(actor, org)
    require market_is_new: not MarketCurrency(org: org, market: market, ..)
    admit MarketCurrency(org, market, currency)

-- Set a book's cap, or replace the one it has. The retract removes the
-- standing cap if there is one and does nothing if there is none.
-- A book with no cap is uncapped. Lowering a cap does not undo trades
-- already in the book. It only limits the next one.
transformation set_position_limit(org, book, cap):
    require may_set_limit: MaySetLimit(actor, org)
    retract PositionLimit(org: org, book: book, ..)
    admit PositionLimit(org, book, cap)

-- Capture a trade: its identity and its first terms, in force from the
-- trade date.
-- The delivery window must run forwards, last at most a year (8784
-- hours, a leap year) and be whole hours. `hours` is the start of every
-- hour the window touches. A whole-hour window touches exactly as many
-- hours as it is long, so a trade starting at half past is refused.
-- Then the cap is checked in each of those hours. With no cap set, that
-- check passes.
transformation capture_trade(org, book, trade, counterparty, market, direction, version, quantity, price, delivery_start, delivery_end, trade_date):
    require may_capture_trade: MayCaptureTrade(actor, org, book)
    require market_has_a_currency: MarketCurrency(org: org, market: market, ..)
    require trade_is_new: not TradeCaptured(trade: trade, ..)
    require terms_version_is_new: not TradeTerms(version: version, ..)
    require delivery_is_forward: delivery_start strictly_before delivery_end
    require delivery_is_at_most_a_year: delivery_end - delivery_start no_longer_than duration(PT8784H)
    let hours = periods(delivery_start, delivery_end, duration(PT1H))
    require delivery_is_whole_hours: (delivery_end - delivery_start) / duration(PT1H) = sum(1 | h in hours)
    let signed = if(direction = #buy, quantity, 0 MW - quantity)
    require hour_within_limit: (forall cap in PositionLimit(org, book, cap): forall h in hours:
        hour_is_within_cap(org, book, trade_date, trade, signed, h, cap))
    admit TradeCaptured(org, book, trade, counterparty, market, direction)
    admit TradeTerms(org, trade, version, quantity, price, delivery_start, delivery_end, trade_date)

-- Amend a trade's terms. The new version sits beside the old one and
-- takes effect on a later date. Only the latest version can be amended.
-- Whoever may capture in the book may amend in it. The window and the
-- cap are checked as at capture.
transformation amend_trade(org, trade, prior_version, new_version, quantity, price, delivery_start, delivery_end, effective_from):
    bind trade_is_captured: TradeCaptured(org, book, trade, _, _, direction)
    require may_amend_trade: MayCaptureTrade(actor, org, book)
    require amendment_takes_effect_later: TradeTerms(org: org, trade: trade, version: prior_version, effective_from: prior_from, ..)
    and effective_from after prior_from
    require prior_terms_are_the_latest: not TradeTermsSupersedes(prior_version: prior_version, ..)
    require terms_version_is_new: not TradeTerms(version: new_version, ..)
    require delivery_is_forward: delivery_start strictly_before delivery_end
    require delivery_is_at_most_a_year: delivery_end - delivery_start no_longer_than duration(PT8784H)
    let hours = periods(delivery_start, delivery_end, duration(PT1H))
    require delivery_is_whole_hours: (delivery_end - delivery_start) / duration(PT1H) = sum(1 | h in hours)
    let signed = if(direction = #buy, quantity, 0 MW - quantity)
    require hour_within_limit: (forall cap in PositionLimit(org, book, cap): forall h in hours:
        hour_is_within_cap(org, book, effective_from, trade, signed, h, cap))
    admit TradeTerms(org, trade, new_version, quantity, price, delivery_start, delivery_end, effective_from)
    admit TradeTermsSupersedes(new_version, prior_version)

-- Register the first curve for a market and date, and make it official.
-- If one is already official, this is refused: use correct_curve.
transformation register_curve(org, market, as_of, version, payload_hash):
    require may_register_curve: MayRegisterCurve(actor, org, market)
    require market_has_a_currency: MarketCurrency(org: org, market: market, ..)
    require curve_version_is_new: not CurveRegistered(version: version, ..)
    require no_official_curve_yet: not OfficialCurve(org: org, market: market, as_of: as_of, ..)
    admit CurveRegistered(org, market, as_of, version, payload_hash)
    admit OfficialCurve(org, market, as_of, version)

-- Correct the official curve. The new version is registered, linked to
-- the one it replaces, and becomes official. The old version and every
-- mark made against it stay on the record.
transformation correct_curve(org, market, as_of, prior_version, new_version, payload_hash):
    require may_register_curve: MayRegisterCurve(actor, org, market)
    require prior_curve_is_official: OfficialCurve(org, market, as_of, prior_version)
    require prior_curve_is_the_latest: not CurveSupersedes(prior_version: prior_version, ..)
    require curve_version_is_new: not CurveRegistered(version: new_version, ..)
    admit CurveRegistered(org, market, as_of, new_version, payload_hash)
    admit CurveSupersedes(new_version, prior_version)
    retract OfficialCurve(org, market, as_of, prior_version)
    admit OfficialCurve(org, market, as_of, new_version)

-- Record a mark-to-market. The number is computed outside the ledger.
-- The ledger checks what it was computed from: the curve version must
-- be the official one for the trade's market right now, and the terms
-- version must be the one in force on that curve's date. A mark against
-- a stale curve or the wrong terms cannot be recorded.
-- The mark says which currency it is in, and that must be the currency
-- of the trade's market. Trade and curve share a market, so they share
-- a currency already. The mark is the number that comes from outside.
-- The patterns of a gate share one `require` because a name bound in
-- one pattern (`market`, `as_of`) is only visible within that `require`.
-- That is also why the currency gate looks the trade's market up again,
-- under its own name.
transformation admit_valuation(org, book, trade, curve_version, terms_version, mtm, currency):
    require may_value_trade: MayValueTrade(actor, org, book)
    require valued_against_official_curve_and_terms_in_force: TradeCaptured(org: org, book: book, trade: trade, market: market, ..)
    and OfficialCurve(org: org, market: market, as_of: as_of, version: curve_version)
    and trade_terms_in_force_on(trade: trade, as_of: as_of, org: org, version: terms_version, ..)
    require mark_is_in_market_currency: TradeCaptured(org: org, trade: trade, market: traded_in, ..)
    and MarketCurrency(org: org, market: traded_in, currency: currency)
    require valuation_is_new: not TradeValued(trade: trade, curve_version: curve_version, terms_version: terms_version, ..)
    admit TradeValued(org, book, trade, curve_version, terms_version, mtm, currency)
